// gx make docs/examples/make_todo_api.gx
//
// This is a GX Make spec — it describes a project for `gx make` to build.
// Run:
//   gx make docs/examples/make_todo_api.gx
//
// Output: a complete Node.js REST API ready to run.

Make "todo-api"

Description:
  A REST API for managing a todo list.
  Built with Node.js and Express (no database — in-memory storage).
  Supports full CRUD: create, read, update, delete todos.

Stack:
  Runtime: Node.js
  Framework: Express
  Storage: in-memory array
  Port: 3000

Endpoints:
  GET    /todos          — list all todos (supports ?done=true/false filter)
  GET    /todos/:id      — get one todo by id
  POST   /todos          — create todo (body: { "text": "Buy milk" })
  PUT    /todos/:id      — update todo (body: { "text": "...", "done": true })
  DELETE /todos/:id      — delete todo

Response format:
  All responses are JSON.
  Success: { "ok": true, "data": ... }
  Error:   { "ok": false, "error": "message" }

Files to generate:
  server.js     — Express server with all routes and middleware
  package.json  — name, version, scripts, express dependency
  .gitignore    — node_modules, .env
  README.md     — setup instructions, curl examples for every endpoint
